Fix Berkeley DB 6.2.32 build with GCC 15 (C23 default standard).

DB_CONFIG callbacks with differing prototypes are stored in a single generic
function-pointer slot, CFG_DESC.func (src/env/env_config.c), and each is called
only after being cast back to its exact prototype selected by CFG_DESC.type in
__config_set_param().  The slot was declared K&R-style as `int (*func)()`.

Under C11/C17 an empty parameter list meant "unspecified arguments", so the
config_descs[] table could initialize that slot with differently-typed
functions directly.  GCC 15 defaults to C23, where an empty parameter list
means "(void)"; the 48 table initializers therefore become
-Wincompatible-pointer-types errors (an error by default since GCC 14), the
first at env_config.c:77, and the build stops at env_config.lo.

This makes the storage type explicit (`int (*func)(void)`) and converts each
initializer to that type through a CFG_FN() cast.  Because every use still
casts func back to the real prototype before calling, the round-trip function-
pointer conversion is well defined (C17/C23 6.3.2.3p8); no diagnostics are
silenced and the struct layout / library ABI are unchanged.

Upstream Berkeley DB 6.2.32 (2017) is unmaintained, so this is carried as a
distro patch.  Scope: src/env/env_config.c only.

--- a/src/env/env_config.c
+++ b/src/env/env_config.c
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
 typedef struct __db_config_desc {
 	char *name;		/* The name of a simple DB_CONFIG command. */
 	__db_config_type type;	/* The enum describing its argument type(s). */
-	int (*func)();		/* The function to call with the argument(s). */
+	int (*func)(void);	/* The function to call with the argument(s). */
 } CFG_DESC;
 
 /* These typedefs help eliminate lint warnings where "func" above is used. */
@@ -59,6 +59,17 @@
 typedef int (*CFG_FUNC_2UINT) __P((DB_ENV *, u_int32_t, u_int32_t));
 
 /*
+ * Every callback below is stored in the generic CFG_DESC.func slot and is
+ * invoked only after being cast back to its exact prototype (selected by
+ * CFG_DESC.type in __config_set_param()), so the round-trip conversion is well
+ * defined.  C11/C17 treated an empty parameter list as "unspecified
+ * arguments", which let these differently-typed functions initialize func
+ * directly.  C23 (the GCC 15 default) redefines an empty parameter list as
+ * "(void)", so the initializers must convert to func's type explicitly.
+ */
+#define	CFG_FN(f)	((int (*)(void))(f))
